{
  "requirement": "Validation MUST read the mdBook source directory from `[book].src` in `book.toml`, using `src` when the setting is absent. It MUST report an unreadable or malformed book configuration and reject an empty, absolute, or parent-traversing source path.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: the requirement is met.**\n\n**Implementation.** `book_source_dir` in `src/evidence.rs` (lines 303–354) is marked `{impl}` for `requirements.ci.book_source`. It does what the requirement says:\n- **Reading the setting.** It reads `book.toml` from the repository root and parses it with `toml_edit`. It takes `[book].src`, and also accepts the inline form `book = { src = … }`.\n- **Default.** It uses `\"src\"` only when `[book]` or `src` is absent.\n- **Unreadable or malformed configuration.** It pushes a diagnostic in each case:\n  - a read failure gives \"cannot read book configuration\";\n  - invalid TOML gives \"invalid TOML\";\n  - a non-table `book` gives \"book must be a table\";\n  - a non-string `src` gives \"book.src must be a string\".\n- **Rejected paths.** An empty `src`, or any path with a component other than `Normal` or `CurDir`, is rejected. That excludes absolute paths (RootDir and Prefix) and parent-traversing paths (ParentDir, including `md/../outside`).\n\n`load_definitions` (lines 141–157) is also marked `{impl}`. It runs `book_source_dir` and turns the collected errors into an `InvalidData` error. `inspect_repository_with_progress` also calls `book_source_dir` and adds its errors to the validation report, so the check runs in the validation path. That function is not marked `{impl}` for this requirement. I accept that because it only delegates to the marked function.\n\nAfter an error, `book_source_dir` returns `root.join(\"md\")` as a placeholder so later checks can continue. The requirement does not specify this fallback. I consider it a minor, benign choice, because the error is already recorded and validation fails.\n\n**Tests.**\n- **Dedicated test.** `book_source_defaults_only_when_absent_and_reports_invalid_configuration` (`src/evidence.rs`, lines 1463–1514) is marked `{test}`. It covers these cases:\n  - **Default.** Empty file; `[book]` without `src`.\n  - **Explicit value.** `src = 'docs'`; the inline-table form.\n  - **Unreadable.** Missing file.\n  - **Malformed.** Invalid TOML; non-table `book`; `src` as integer, boolean, array and table; empty, absolute, `../` and `md/../` paths.\n- **Integration test.** `validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` also carries a `{test}` marker and exercises the validation path end to end.\n- **Other tests.** `configuration_and_dependency_failures_do_not_stop_later_checks` checks that an invalid `book.toml` is reported through `validate_repository` alongside other errors.\n\nI found no gaps. The boundaries and failure modes the requirement names are all covered.",
